course: dictionary
lesson: 5997
title: Measurable: can you measure it?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Measurable means able to be measured. A ruler can measure a pencil, so the pencil's length is measurable.
explain: Measurable can also mean big enough to be noticed. In «The Atacama Desert in Chile is the driest non-polar desert, and some of its weather stations have never recorded measurable rain», the rain is so small or so rare that the stations never got an amount they could measure.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "Never recorded rain big enough to be measured" still makes sense, so measurable means that here.
fact: Measurable means able to be measured.
fact: Measurable can also mean big enough to be noticed, like a measurable difference.
fact: Measurable is an adjective, a word that describes a noun.
fact: In school, measurable progress means you can show how much better you have become.
fact: The Atacama Desert in Chile is the driest non-polar desert, and its dry soil is so much like Mars that scientists test Mars rovers there.
exercise: What does measurable mean? | Very loud | *Able to be measured | Full of colour | Hard to climb
exercise: «Some weather stations in the Atacama have never recorded measurable rain.» What does this suggest about the rain? | *It was too little to be measured | It fell every single day | It was a huge storm that flooded the town | It was made of gold
exercise: Ms Patel says the class has made measurable progress in reading. What does measurable progress mean? | You have stopped reading for the year | You read only in the dark | You have finished every book in the library | *You can show how much better you have become
test: Measurable is which part of speech? | Verb | *Adjective | Noun | Adverb
test: In «a measurable difference», measurable means: | Very far away | Too small to see | *Big enough to be noticed | Made of metal
exam: In «measurable rain» from the Atacama sentence, what does measurable mean? | Rain that smells sweet | *Rain big enough to be measured | Rain falling sideways | Rain that is warm
